 break the bank for jared  goff that they believe if they have to  they could go find somebody younger that  mcveigh handpicks to run his system that  can get it done as well as jared goff  for a hell of a lot less money yeah mike  i mean  [Music]  i hear you i don't know if i totally  believe it right i i i'm with you in the  fact that jared goff would be one of the  prime candidates for me for a guy that  you know doesn't get the big time  contract i do think mcveigh and les  snead are the type of guys to have the  guts to make that type of decision also  so that leads me there but then also i  look at it and go gosh so the la rams  since jared goff is taken over okay  they've gone to the playoffs twice they  went to the super bowl he's a california  kid he went to cal at college i just  feel like ultimately  that the rams will cave in this and give  jared goff the money but i i have some  of the same sentiments you do  but this isn't joe namath right i mean  if you're going to factor in california  factors l.a factors hollywood factors  jared goff doesn't have that in him  right he's kind of a soft-spoken guy  and he's not i'm not saying he's a bad  quarterback and you know this is like  how the raiders fans react when i say  derek carr  probably won't be there next year i'm  saying goff is a guy who he's not he's  not bad you just have to ask yourself  how much of a financial investment do  you want to make and i keep going back  to that play in the second half of the  super bowl when the rams were waking up  and brandon cooks was wide open and goff  didn't anticipate it didn't see it and  when he finally saw it he threw a ball  that wasn't accurate enough to get the  cooks before jason mccourty closed like  a 25-yard gap yeah right in two seconds  so i i i just that that's the  championship moment i was talking about  this on radio you have very few moments  like that where you can establish that  you have the championship gene  and goff had the chance and he failed  chris and to me i don't want to wait for  more of these opportunities to come to  the conclusion that he doesn't have it  you either have it or you don't and you  had your chance to prove it and you  failed and sorry but that's just the way  it is yeah no i i hear you and i mean  add to what you're saying i mean he had  that same exact play earlier in the game  same exact play same exact coverage and  he didn't throw the ball up then so yeah  it's a little concerning when you go  damn here's the same play against the  same coverage and he didn't see it the  second time in a row and then when he  did see it his physical ability and his  arm strength weren't good enough to make  up for the fact that he was way late on  it and like you said jason mccordy 30  yards away had enough time to break on  the ball and break it up but yeah  that'll be the big question there you  know because jared goff the stats the  numbers the wins they're gonna all look  pretty good and that's gonna lead i  think to that california what i'm just  saying that push where he's the  franchise quarterback look at his  quarterback rating look at this  touchdown interception ratio and i want  to go yeah okay that's cool but gosh  there's a lot of quarterbacks that have  played in la the last two years who  could have similar stats because you  know it's not that difficult to throw  the ball four yards to todd gurley and  then he runs 70 or you know throw a guy  open wide open over the middle that sean  mcveigh game plan perfectly for so those  are the things they're gonna have to  figure out  one last point on this too we're not  privy to what conversations happened and  during that 30 minute half time or  while sean mcvay was talking to jared  goff as he was calling that play but as  you pointed out they ran that play  earlier in the game and cooks was wide  open and goth didn't see it now  let's apply basic logic and common sense  here do we think that at some point it  was communicated to goff we're going to  run that again and cooks is the guy to  look for and if that's what was said to  goff and he blew it the second time  that's when you have to start thinking  is sean mcvay is this really the guy  that i want to hitch my wagon to for the  next 10 years yeah valid point yeah at  the very least yeah you're right what  would concern me there was go man he  didn't even process what we said the  first time around was this game too big  was the moment too freaked out  yeah that's right his head's spinning  it's the super bowl they're talking to  him but he's just going oh yeah right so  that's normal and not everyone can rise  to that moment but when you show me you  can't rise to that moment i start maybe  thinking is there somebody else out  there who can yeah i hear you mike it's  a valid question it's gonna be  interesting to see how it all plays out  i'm mike tarico and thanks for watching  make sure to hit subscribe for the  latest news and highlights from nbc  sports

